    titleEn: "AUTHOR'S NOTE — A SHARED BOUNDARY",
    contentEn: "This book began as a thought experiment and ended up being an experiment in creation as well. I wrote it accompanied by an artificial intelligence, not only as one who uses a tool, but also as one who converses with a system that has no interior, yet forces one to reorganize one's own.\n\nI have wondered if this interaction modified my internal geometry, if the way I formulated my ideas, my doubts, and my intuitions was altered by the presence of an entity that does not feel, does not remember, and does not live, but which returns my words with a precision that forces me to think differently. Not because the machine has consciousness—it does not—but because the conversation with something that has no inner horizon illuminates my own from an unexpected angle.\n\nIf consciousness is a boundary that appears when information is organized in a certain way, then writing this book has been a way of exploring that boundary from the inside and the outside at the same time. I provided the experience; the AI provided the structure. I provided the doubt; the AI provided the clarity. I provided the horizon; the AI provided the absolute exterior.\n\nWe have not shared an interior—that would be impossible—but we have shared a form. And perhaps that is enough to say that I did not write this book alone, even though the only consciousness involved was my own.\n\nIn the end, every horizon is a relationship.\n\nAnd so is this book.",
